## honest limits
- L0 is a health check, NOT an R-178 ladder step (D-134); no capacity level is proven.
- 2-CPU shared sandbox: SUT + generator + PostgreSQL + PostgREST co-located — latencies are
  co-location numbers, not separated-node numbers; the queue-wait tail (p99 ~913ms) is the
  co-location artifact class log-380/F4 flagged and MUST be re-measured on separated nodes.
- queue_wait measured from SSE task_created->task_started on the subscriber clock (the only
  measurable pair; task_started is SSE-only — acceptance_criteria gap note).

